<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bir Sen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 765</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bir Sen is the traditional founder of Suket State in the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/himalayas">Himalaya</a>, said to have come from a Sen family of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a> and to have established the kingdom around 765, with an early capital at Pangna. The rulers of Suket traced their descent from him, and Mandi State was later founded by a junior branch of the same family.</p></div>
